-foreach is an array function which is used for its side affect result not for return since it returns always undefined so if we want to see its result we need to make the element that we have made changes on it in the console otherwise if we assign a refernce to the foreach the result will be undefined.
-foreach doesnt return a result of the operation like deleting from the array and so on but it always return undefined.
-here if we do const o = req.query o and req.query both of them are refrences to the same object so if we made changes on one of them the other will be affected instead if we use the spread operator (...) in this case we are creating a copy of this object that s all, we call this copy shallow copy.
-when you use foreach you are interested on the side effect performed with the callback rather than the return.
-if you assign a variable to the result of foreach this variable will be undefined.
-Exactly! The \b in regular expressions is used to match positions where a word character (like letters, digits, or underscores) is next to a non-word character (like spaces, punctuation, or other symbols), in this case if we take catalogue and cat! and the regular expression is \bcat\b then cat! is matched.
