-You cannot use await directly in the global scope or in non-async functions. Wrapping the code in an async function allows you to use await to handle asynchronous operations.
-we hash the tokens If someone gains access to your database, they shouldn't be able to retrieve sensitive information like tokens. By hashing the token, even if the database is exposed, the actual reset token is not available in plain text.
-If the reset token is stored in plain text, an attacker with access to the database can use it directly to reset any user's password without needing their email or authorization, then he can use it in the url of the setting of the password eventhough he dont need to access the email by doing the following  https://yourwebsite.com/reset-password?token=abcd1234efgh5678.
