-Local installation of packages involves adding them to your project's node_modules directory, making them available only within that specific project. You install local packages with the command npm install <package-name> --save-dev and can use them through npm scripts defined in your package.json or with npx. This approach helps manage dependencies on a per-project basis and avoids conflicts between projects. In contrast, global installation installs packages system-wide, allowing you to use them from anywhere on your system with the command npm install -g <package-name>. This is convenient for tools and utilities used across multiple projects, but it does not manage versions on a per-project basis. Using local installation helps ensure consistent dependencies and avoids potential issues with different project requirements.
-for the devdependencies we use them only in the phase of developping  and testing phases of your project. They are not required for your application to run in production , we use them more in our terminal to customize it they are for testing to make them present in the devdependencies we must use the --save-dev option, nodemon, eslint, or jest.
